[[:db/retract 17592186180100 :question/answer-fields 17592186178269] [:db/retract 17592186180101 :question/answer-fields 17592186178275] [:db/retract 17592186180105 :question/answer-fields 17592186178299] [:db/retract 17592186180106 :question/answer-fields 17592186178305] [:db/retract 17592186180107 :question/answer-fields 17592186178311] {:db/id 17592186179777 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cc2329ee-2286-5cc1-b9c4-aaae4fcfd160" "question-49e23a3c-f5ee-5f32-8207-650dc0b4ca07" "question-539e0059-24fe-5c3a-b9b6-abd2934de330" "question-0be1c169-3c4d-5e81-bcd5-f050f3ef61f9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179778 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7a6ac8ce-563c-538e-a4b6-829308c43be7" "question-2dec6491-4f2e-5985-9f0d-5f140c0cfaf3" "question-fdc532fe-5376-523b-b4c1-4852cb3ef3ca" "question-115c519a-042d-5002-84f6-473dd06e56ff"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179779 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-34ad571d-a040-5724-a4dd-5d1ff6b4a0c6" "question-6813bd80-c67c-56a5-8d0d-2e4e5ee1b618" "question-d148a18c-482f-58b6-ae26-c16e793a32c1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179780 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-841964b0-d48f-583c-9b1a-d5d38816deaf" "question-e08604c1-4714-50ad-b1df-f5621c3586f5" "question-a80bea3f-8cb9-59ff-8c63-3325a8f0a338"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cc2329ee-2286-5cc1-b9c4-aaae4fcfd160" :question/id #uuid "cc2329ee-2286-5cc1-b9c4-aaae4fcfd160" :question/math-academy-id "q-163682" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis under the action of a force of magnitude $(2-x)\\,\\text{N}$ acting in the direction of increasing $x.$ Given that $x$ is measured in meters, calculate the work done by the force in moving the particle from $x=1$ to $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The work done by a force $F=F(x)$ in moving a particle from $x={x}_{1}$ to $x={x}_{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nW={\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}F(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhen the force and distance are measured in Newtons and meters, respectively, the work done by the force is measured in Joules ($J$).\n\nSubstituting the given values into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2(2)-\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{2})-(2(1)-\\frac{1}{2}({1}^{2})) \\\\  & =4-2-2+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,J.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f0260c4e-12d5-5629-b2d4-7c1539134366"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f0260c4e-12d5-5629-b2d4-7c1539134366" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0260c4e-12d5-5629-b2d4-7c1539134366" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-917167c2-f28e-5235-8996-88a317199397" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bb2d71f8-f520-5950-a0fc-eaf5e6853af6" "answer-e9148945-fdec-553f-9907-9d2484cbc0ed" "answer-4f15786c-7b03-54e6-8703-5ed8327eeb6f" "answer-917167c2-f28e-5235-8996-88a317199397" "answer-f75d04ef-9f29-5e3a-9b0c-022da6954dc5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb2d71f8-f520-5950-a0fc-eaf5e6853af6" :answer/id #uuid "bb2d71f8-f520-5950-a0fc-eaf5e6853af6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9148945-fdec-553f-9907-9d2484cbc0ed" :answer/id #uuid "e9148945-fdec-553f-9907-9d2484cbc0ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f15786c-7b03-54e6-8703-5ed8327eeb6f" :answer/id #uuid "4f15786c-7b03-54e6-8703-5ed8327eeb6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-917167c2-f28e-5235-8996-88a317199397" :answer/id #uuid "917167c2-f28e-5235-8996-88a317199397" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f75d04ef-9f29-5e3a-9b0c-022da6954dc5" :answer/id #uuid "f75d04ef-9f29-5e3a-9b0c-022da6954dc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-49e23a3c-f5ee-5f32-8207-650dc0b4ca07" :question/id #uuid "49e23a3c-f5ee-5f32-8207-650dc0b4ca07" :question/math-academy-id "q-163686" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis under the action of a force of magnitude $(3\\sqrt{x}+2)\\,\\text{N}$ acting in the direction of increasing $x.$ Given that $x$ is measured in meters, calculate the work done by the force in moving the particle from $x=1$ to $x=4.$" :question/worked-solution "The work done by a force $F=F(x)$ in moving a particle from $x={x}_{1}$ to $x={x}_{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nW={\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}F(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhen the force and distance are measured in Newtons and meters, respectively, the work done by the force is measured in Joules ($J$).\n\nSubstituting the given values into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(3\\sqrt{x}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(3{x}^{1/2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3/2}+2x]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =2({4}^{3/2})+2(4)-(2({1}^{3/2})+2(1)) \\\\  & =16+8-2-2 \\\\  & =20\\,J.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e533a5eb-946c-53fd-b9db-7dca4ec6140a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e533a5eb-946c-53fd-b9db-7dca4ec6140a" :answer-field/id #uuid "e533a5eb-946c-53fd-b9db-7dca4ec6140a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bf2651a2-6940-5df5-b549-821bd938e2ae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d88f3206-b7d8-5454-a54b-c8dbf5728dd6" "answer-944d02a9-bd37-50e5-8f3a-13e10492e0a6" "answer-6e01e9e2-099f-5829-bb90-988331fa2c4e" "answer-bf2651a2-6940-5df5-b549-821bd938e2ae" "answer-afa584ba-d9c9-5af5-875d-b8761e92e385"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d88f3206-b7d8-5454-a54b-c8dbf5728dd6" :answer/id #uuid "d88f3206-b7d8-5454-a54b-c8dbf5728dd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-944d02a9-bd37-50e5-8f3a-13e10492e0a6" :answer/id #uuid "944d02a9-bd37-50e5-8f3a-13e10492e0a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e01e9e2-099f-5829-bb90-988331fa2c4e" :answer/id #uuid "6e01e9e2-099f-5829-bb90-988331fa2c4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf2651a2-6940-5df5-b549-821bd938e2ae" :answer/id #uuid "bf2651a2-6940-5df5-b549-821bd938e2ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afa584ba-d9c9-5af5-875d-b8761e92e385" :answer/id #uuid "afa584ba-d9c9-5af5-875d-b8761e92e385" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-539e0059-24fe-5c3a-b9b6-abd2934de330" :question/id #uuid "539e0059-24fe-5c3a-b9b6-abd2934de330" :question/math-academy-id "q-163688" :question/problem "A particle $P$ of mass $0.5\\,kg$ moves along the $x$-axis with an acceleration of magnitude $(5-x)\\,{m/s}^{2}$ acting in the direction $OP.$ Given that $x$ is measured in meters, calculate the work done by the force in moving the particle from $x=1$ to $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The work done by a force $F=F(x)$ in moving a particle from $x={x}_{1}$ to $x={x}_{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nW={\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}F(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhen the force and distance are measured in Newtons and meters, respectively, the work done by the force is measured in Joules ($J$).\n\nUsing Newton's second law of motion, the force required to accelerate a particle of mass $0.5\\,kg$ at a rate of $(5-x)\\,{m/s}^{2}$ is\n\n$$\nF=ma=0.5\\cdot (5-x)=(2.5-0.5x)\\,N.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the known values into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(2.5-0.5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{5}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(2)-\\frac{1}{4}({2}^{2})-(\\frac{5}{2}(1)-\\frac{1}{4}({1}^{2})) \\\\  & =5-1-\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}\\,J.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6d665a14-f9c6-5b0e-9f42-6dea1fa5cd93"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6d665a14-f9c6-5b0e-9f42-6dea1fa5cd93" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d665a14-f9c6-5b0e-9f42-6dea1fa5cd93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7e2f1ede-2cc2-54bb-8896-41a7f39dd5ec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4906765c-cf5e-56de-b7cc-bbfeff0afa63" "answer-1ed38dcf-d565-5c8f-a354-7f15129024b7" "answer-78e2fabc-a95e-59e5-9e2c-304ec9d164ae" "answer-fc464ecd-6249-5343-9b2d-d1ebf3f3d163" "answer-7e2f1ede-2cc2-54bb-8896-41a7f39dd5ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4906765c-cf5e-56de-b7cc-bbfeff0afa63" :answer/id #uuid "4906765c-cf5e-56de-b7cc-bbfeff0afa63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ed38dcf-d565-5c8f-a354-7f15129024b7" :answer/id #uuid "1ed38dcf-d565-5c8f-a354-7f15129024b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78e2fabc-a95e-59e5-9e2c-304ec9d164ae" :answer/id #uuid "78e2fabc-a95e-59e5-9e2c-304ec9d164ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc464ecd-6249-5343-9b2d-d1ebf3f3d163" :answer/id #uuid "fc464ecd-6249-5343-9b2d-d1ebf3f3d163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e2f1ede-2cc2-54bb-8896-41a7f39dd5ec" :answer/id #uuid "7e2f1ede-2cc2-54bb-8896-41a7f39dd5ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180100 :question/problem "A particle $P$ of mass $1.5\\,kg$ moves along the $x$-axis with an acceleration of magnitude $(2x+1)\\,{m/s}^{2}$ acting in the direction $OP.$ Given that $x$ is measured in meters, calculate the work done by the force in moving the particle from $x=1$ to $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The work done by a force $F=F(x)$ in moving a particle from $x={x}_{1}$ to $x={x}_{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nW={\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}F(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhen the force and distance are measured in Newtons and meters, respectively, the work done by the force is measured in Joules ($J$).\n\nUsing Newton's second law of motion, the force required to accelerate a particle of mass $1.5\\,kg$ at a rate of $(2x+1)\\,{m/s}^{2}$ is\n\n$$\nF=ma=1.5\\cdot (2x+1)=(3x+1.5)\\,N.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the known values into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3x+1.5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}x]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}({2}^{2}+2-({1}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(6-2) \\\\  & =6\\,J.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-188254e6-7bf6-52e7-85b7-577eb0a8ea66"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-188254e6-7bf6-52e7-85b7-577eb0a8ea66" :answer-field/id #uuid "188254e6-7bf6-52e7-85b7-577eb0a8ea66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3b968cb6-6ae9-5b0c-9af4-6dd1a21d39c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8b758d59-3144-5ba6-9ee7-ab705a9dc58e" "answer-ebdc4bfd-1d77-5007-a2a4-775aba359b33" "answer-6afd05e0-6e50-556e-93ad-2b191ada987b" "answer-469e84d9-10e8-5bb8-8014-4bea0369b746" "answer-3b968cb6-6ae9-5b0c-9af4-6dd1a21d39c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b758d59-3144-5ba6-9ee7-ab705a9dc58e" :answer/id #uuid "8b758d59-3144-5ba6-9ee7-ab705a9dc58e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebdc4bfd-1d77-5007-a2a4-775aba359b33" :answer/id #uuid "ebdc4bfd-1d77-5007-a2a4-775aba359b33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6afd05e0-6e50-556e-93ad-2b191ada987b" :answer/id #uuid "6afd05e0-6e50-556e-93ad-2b191ada987b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-469e84d9-10e8-5bb8-8014-4bea0369b746" :answer/id #uuid "469e84d9-10e8-5bb8-8014-4bea0369b746" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b968cb6-6ae9-5b0c-9af4-6dd1a21d39c6" :answer/id #uuid "3b968cb6-6ae9-5b0c-9af4-6dd1a21d39c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0be1c169-3c4d-5e81-bcd5-f050f3ef61f9" :question/id #uuid "0be1c169-3c4d-5e81-bcd5-f050f3ef61f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-163687" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis under the action of a force of magnitude $(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{N}$ acting in the direction of increasing $x.$ Given that $x$ is measured in meters, calculate the work done by the force in moving the particle from $x=1$ to $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The work done by a force $F=F(x)$ in moving a particle from $x={x}_{1}$ to $x={x}_{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nW={\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}F(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhen the force and distance are measured in Newtons and meters, respectively, the work done by the force is measured in Joules ($J$).\n\nSubstituting the given values into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[8x-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =8(2)-\\frac{1}{4}({2}^{4})-(8(1)-\\frac{1}{4}({1}^{4})) \\\\  & =16-4-8+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{4}\\,J.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ecf8557a-f127-5151-95f4-647459864ef1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ecf8557a-f127-5151-95f4-647459864ef1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecf8557a-f127-5151-95f4-647459864ef1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a609468-13c4-5167-adfa-d9641c742919" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d8495461-fbf1-5db5-90d6-ecc9dfa46e3c" "answer-2a35d382-4f29-517d-8811-38dd718f3949" "answer-9c755c70-2778-53b1-aa2d-fd52ee0d754b" "answer-6a609468-13c4-5167-adfa-d9641c742919" "answer-7fb1a335-16df-592b-9aa2-30cdc25d7546"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8495461-fbf1-5db5-90d6-ecc9dfa46e3c" :answer/id #uuid "d8495461-fbf1-5db5-90d6-ecc9dfa46e3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a35d382-4f29-517d-8811-38dd718f3949" :answer/id #uuid "2a35d382-4f29-517d-8811-38dd718f3949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c755c70-2778-53b1-aa2d-fd52ee0d754b" :answer/id #uuid "9c755c70-2778-53b1-aa2d-fd52ee0d754b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a609468-13c4-5167-adfa-d9641c742919" :answer/id #uuid "6a609468-13c4-5167-adfa-d9641c742919" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fb1a335-16df-592b-9aa2-30cdc25d7546" :answer/id #uuid "7fb1a335-16df-592b-9aa2-30cdc25d7546" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180101 :question/problem "A particle $P$ of mass $2\\,kg$ moves along the $x$-axis from rest at the origin with an acceleration of magnitude $2t\\,{m/s}^{2},$ where the acceleration acts in the direction of increasing $x,$ and $t\\ge 0$ is the time in seconds. Calculate the particle's kinetic energy at time $t=2\\,s.$" :question/worked-solution "The kinetic energy of a particle with mass $m$ and velocity $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{KE}=\\frac{1}{2}m{v}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWhen the mass and velocity are measured in kilograms and meters per second, respectively, the particle's kinetic energy is measured in Joules ($J$).\n\nFirst, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ v(t) & =\\int 2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ v(t) & ={t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(0)=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n0={0}^{2}+C\\,⟹\\,C=0.\n$$\n\nHence, the velocity of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)={t}^{2}.$ In particular, its velocity at time $t=2\\,s$ is\n\n$$\nv=v(2)={2}^{2}=4\\,m/s.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the kinetic energy of the particle at $t=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{KE} & =\\frac{1}{2}m{v}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot {4}^{2} \\\\  & =16\\,J.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cb6dfeb2-3a92-53e8-a0f6-ee617bbb1e9c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb6dfeb2-3a92-53e8-a0f6-ee617bbb1e9c" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb6dfeb2-3a92-53e8-a0f6-ee617bbb1e9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-832666e4-bfb7-5311-860f-b9c7edf6df68" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ef25fa57-c8c1-5068-8f4b-f19cebf60716" "answer-b8a7e4a3-4075-524e-b699-5f80dc6c213a" "answer-832666e4-bfb7-5311-860f-b9c7edf6df68" "answer-0c59d75c-f137-5ad0-adb1-d98444184b0b" "answer-112a9bb0-329a-50bc-862b-f1f1908e9ef2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef25fa57-c8c1-5068-8f4b-f19cebf60716" :answer/id #uuid "ef25fa57-c8c1-5068-8f4b-f19cebf60716" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8a7e4a3-4075-524e-b699-5f80dc6c213a" :answer/id #uuid "b8a7e4a3-4075-524e-b699-5f80dc6c213a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\,J" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-832666e4-